    "created_at": "2023-12-13T03:48:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-12-13T03:54:41Z",
    "body": "Just throwing my weight that this is **not** the right place to standardize this. Also just echoing what @RByers said: CGs can produce their own specs (see WICG, which [produces hundreds](https://wicg.io)). \r\n\r\nI'd suggest doing this in a CG, then, if there is enough incentive, ask the W3C to create a \"real\" working group for formal standardization along the W3C Rec Track. \r\n\r\nThe CG process should provide adequate IPR protections for folks participating, and make the transition to formal standardization relatively straight forward.  \r\n\r\nAlso just echoing what @karlcow said: the compat spec should be a place of last resort for documenting/specifying an extremely narrow set of proprietary features (or \"mistakes\", really, that leaked out into the world).  \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
